Files: usr/share/marble/data/maps/*
    The map themes of KDE's Marble map catalogue (https://marble.kde.org/maps-v3.xml), unmodified
    (each one as Marble's "Download Maps" dialog installs it). Licence and credit of each, as the
    catalogue states them:

    Mercury (mercury, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA/SDIO, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program.
    Venus (venus, version 0.3): Public domain. NASA/JPL-Caltech.
    Venus Topography (topomagellan, version 0.2): Public domain. NASA/JPL-Caltech.
    Mars (mars, version 0.4): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program.
    Mars Topography (mgsmola, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program.
    Mars - 1886 - Schiaparelli. (schiaparelli1886, version 0.1): Public domain. Giovanni Schiaparelli
    Mars - 1895 - Lowell. (lowell1895, version 0.1): Public domain. Percival Lowell
    Moon - 1609 - Thomas Harriot (harriot1609, version 0.1): Public domain. Thomas Harriot in 1609.
    Moon - 1645 - Hevelius (hevelius1645, version 0.2): Public domain. Johannes Hevelius in 1645, published in "Selenographia, sive Lunae descriptio".
    Moon - 1707 - Homann and Doppelmayr (doppelmayr1707, version 0.1): Public domain. Homann and Doppelmayr in 1707.
    Moon - Elevation (moonelev, version 0.2): Public domain. NASA/SDIO, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program.
    Moon - Shaded Relief (moonhill, version 0.2): Public domain. NASA, 2002. Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program.
    Jupiter - Europa (jupiter-europa, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program
    Jupiter - Ganymede (jupiter-ganymede, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program
    Saturn - Dione (saturn-dione, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program
    Saturn - Mimas (saturn-mimas, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program
    Saturn - Rhea (saturn-rhea, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA, Courtesy USGS Astrogeology Research Program
    Saturn - Titan (saturn-titan, version 0.1): Public domain. NASA/JPL-Caltech/Space Science Institute

    The themes are packaged by KDE's Marble project (https://marble.kde.org, https://invent.kde.org/education/marble).
